            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "While not as creamy as ice cream made with a cooked custard,this is still pretty darn good and couldn't be easier. I used 2 c. heavy cream and 1 c. half and half as I wanted a bit richer and smoother final result. After tasting the mixture I felt it needed another 1/2 tsp. of root beer extract (I used Watkins) and it was perfect. However, this may or not be the case with other brands of root beer extract or root beer concentrate such as McCormick's, so taste first. It DOES taste like a root beer float!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kristi Howell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I normally make custard-based ice cream and was very impressed with the way this came out. Using my stand mixer, I beat the eggs and sugar for several minutes, then added the extracts, then equal parts heavy cream and fat free half &amp; half. Like most reviewers, I doubled the amount of root beer extract. After freezing and ripening, the texture was perfect and the flavor was heavenly. Plus, so quick and easy!",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-09T15:18:17.093Z"
          },
